Remove the flextaxd dependency: CanSNPer2 now carries its own taxonomy database code

ISSUES #59-#62 (covers #1, #9-#12, #21-#24, #26), #44

- modules/DatabaseConnection.py: ported CreateDatabase, a TaxonomyDBConnection
  (creates a missing database through CreateDatabase instead of calling it as a
  shell script), DatabaseFunctions and ModifyFunctions from flextaxd.
- modules/ModifyTree.py (new): ported tree modification from flextaxd.
- modules/ReadTaxonomyCanSNPer.py (new): the CanSNPer tree reader (semicolon/
  tab lineage format) with its base class, connected to the local DatabaseFunctions.
- modules/WriteTaxonomy.py (new): tab export of tree/annotation for --export.
- InitiateDatabase, ModifyDatabase, NewickTree, SNPDatabase now import from
  CanSNPer2.modules; get_read_modules scans CanSNPer2's own modules directory;
  dynamic_import loads ReadTaxonomy{source_type} from CanSNPer2.modules.
- ModifyDatabase super().__init__ passes separator/verbose/parent/replace as
  keywords (they had landed in ModifyTree's clean_database/purge_database/
  update_genomes positional slots), fixing #44's mod_genomes path.
- setup.py install_requires drops flextaxd; selftest.py and README drop it too.

Verified against the mapped flextaxd sources (read-only): creating the
Francisella database from CanSNPer2-data/source with the ported code produces a
database identical (all nodes/tree/rank rows) to the current flextaxd code, and
a modify run (mod_file, parent B.1) matches flextaxd ModifyTree output; the
tab export files are byte-identical.
